<h1>Ecosystems &amp; Inputs</h1>
<p class="subtitle">OSV matching covers ten ecosystems. Heuristic registry/source analysis is narrower.</p>

<table class="cmd-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Ecosystem</th><th>Preferred input</th><th>Fallback or partial input</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>npm</td><td><code>package-lock.json</code>, <code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code>, <code>yarn.lock</code></td><td><code>package.json</code> has lower confidence</td></tr>
    <tr><td>PyPI</td><td><code>Pipfile.lock</code>, <code>poetry.lock</code></td><td><code>requirements.txt</code>, <code>pyproject.toml</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Cargo</td><td><code>Cargo.lock</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Go</td><td><code>go.mod</code></td><td><code>go.sum</code> is checksum history</td></tr>
    <tr><td>RubyGems</td><td><code>Gemfile.lock</code></td><td><code>Gemfile</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Composer</td><td><code>composer.lock</code></td><td><code>composer.json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>NuGet</td><td><code>packages.lock.json</code></td><td><code>*.csproj</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Java</td><td><code>gradle.lockfile</code></td><td><code>pom.xml</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Hex</td><td><code>mix.lock</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Dart/pub</td><td><code>pubspec.lock</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Discovery</h2>
<p>vexes looks for recognized files at the selected target directory. It is not an arbitrary recursive monorepo crawler. Point <code>--path</code> at the project you intend to scan.</p>

<h2>Completeness and identity</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Resolved lockfiles are preferred. Ruby/PHP/NuGet/Java manifest fallbacks can provide exact pins but are not resolved dependency graphs, so they are marked incomplete.</li>
  <li><code>go.mod</code> is preferred. Replaced modules are excluded and make coverage incomplete; <code>go.sum</code> alone can contain modules no longer active.</li>
  <li>pnpm lockfile major versions 6 and 9 are recognized. Other major shapes fail visibly.</li>
  <li>Ruby lock entries require the canonical RubyGems remote and Bundler SHA-256 checksums; older unchecked locks remain incomplete.</li>
  <li>Malformed or unrecognized shapes are errors, not empty dependency sets.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Analysis support is not the same as scan support</h2>
<p><code>scan</code> uses OSV across the ecosystems above. Registry heuristics and bounded source inspection currently operate on npm/PyPI evidence only. JavaScript samples use an AST; Python samples use lightweight pattern matching. Other ecosystems should not be described as receiving the same four analysis groups.</p>
